-- title:
--   Surjectivity and kernel of the diamond transfer on H¹
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a positive integer, $A$ an abelian group, and $H, H'$ subgroups of $(\mathbb{Z}/L\mathbb{Z})^\times$. For a subgroup $K \le (\mathbb{Z}/L\mathbb{Z})^\times$ write $\Gamma_K(L) =$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH L K`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) for the subgroup of $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$ obtained as the image of the preimage of $K$ under the character $\Gamma_0(L) \to (\mathbb{Z}/L\mathbb{Z})^\times$ sending a matrix to the reduction of its lower right entry, and [`CohCarrier.H1 L K A`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L162) $= \operatorname{Hom}(\Gamma_K(L), A)$ (additive homomorphisms out of the additivisation of $\Gamma_K(L)$). Assume a relation [`CohCarrier.LevelLE L L H' H 1`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L330), whose content here is that $L \mid L$, $1 \mid L/L$, and every $u \in H$ has image in $H'$ under the reduction map attached to $L \mid L$; so $\Gamma_H(L) \le \Gamma_{H'}(L)$. Assume further a divisor $r$ of $L$ with $4 \le r$ such that every $u \in H'$ reduces to $1$ in $\mathbb{Z}/r\mathbb{Z}$. Let $j =$ [`CohCarrier.jDeg L L H' H 1 A h`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L482) $: \operatorname{Hom}(\Gamma_H(L),A) \to \operatorname{Hom}(\Gamma_{H'}(L),A)$ be the additive transfer [`CohCarrier.coresAdd`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L63) applied to the transport of $\varphi$ along the embedding [`CohCarrier.iotaDeg`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L383) of degree $1$. Then $j$ is surjective, and $j(\varphi) = 0$ holds precisely when $\varphi$ lies in the subgroup generated by all differences $\langle\sigma\rangle x - x$, where $x \in \operatorname{Hom}(\Gamma_H(L),A)$, $\sigma \in \Gamma_0(L)$ has image in $\Gamma_{H'}(L)$, and $\langle\sigma\rangle x =$ [`CohCarrier.diamondRaw L H A σ x`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L291) is precomposition of $x$ with conjugation by $\sigma$ on $\Gamma_H(L)$.
--
--   This is the corestriction (trace) map in degree one along the covering of open modular curves $Y_H(L) \to Y_{H'}(L)$, asserted to be surjective with kernel exactly the diamond augmentation subgroup, so that it identifies the coinvariants of $\operatorname{Hom}(\Gamma_H(L),A)$ under the diamond action of $H'/H$ with $\operatorname{Hom}(\Gamma_{H'}(L),A)$; the condition $\Gamma_{H'}(L) \subseteq \Gamma_1(r)$ with $r \ge 4$ guarantees freeness of the ambient group. It is used in the computation of ranks of corner submodules of $H^1$ and in the construction, at Taylor–Wiles levels, of surjections between cohomology modules with prescribed kernel.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CohCarrier_surjective_jDeg_one_and_jDeg_eq_zero_iff_of_four_le.lean

import Mathlib
